;;; A bare `_` inside a nested fact is dropped at load, in silence —
;;; **W29**, regression `nested-fact-arg` (`corpus/regressions.toml`),
;;; under Q-M1e2.22.
;;;
;;;
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; One fact whose first argument is the nested fact `(f _ a)`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; A bare `_` is reserved and names nothing, at any depth (Q-M1e2.22), so the
;;; program is refused at load, with a line naming the place: every command
;;; that reads it exits 1 (`ein test`: 2).
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered, and what it answers ──────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `ec004a48` (the engine `916d97ac`'s), release and debug alike: the
;;; loader dropped the `_` and stored `(r (f a) c)`, with no line. Root's
;;; state was `(model (r (f a) c))` and R four states, over the candidates
;;; `(r a c)` and `(r c a)`, exit 0 (`ein solve FILE`, `ein oracle FILE`).
;;; Today the parse refuses the `_`.

(relation r T T)
(r (f _ a) c)
